{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788623684674749001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"prenatal-maudlin-seahorse","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"3582f66ee70f44fea8dcf7f4461a4678ac72f26fd3a20bab8e61e74f8fa603e8","event_uuid":"09520870-72ee-431a-bb6d-4439fa31c68f","position":{"commit_sha":"4b9bb300802ccf1c49774e43eb4635ddce707a4b","position":"1788621079663951045-09520870-72ee-431a-bb6d-4439fa31c68f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a9a6bde25c118be7996750d3ecf284df3a69ce711753057b3dd7e6f584764edd","event_uuid":"d9e61719-91f9-4f23-99d4-a4a16ed250bf","position":{"commit_sha":"17d6548a33ca4496c36b021ea838b2d63521afaf","position":"1788621530184462718-d9e61719-91f9-4f23-99d4-a4a16ed250bf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e163d145d08e10b02cc584e3643463687f5ba12c540a64bc1f00a8876e7e9e59","event_uuid":"9ea4c2c1-8dd2-4415-8112-6e4c29672829","position":{"commit_sha":"82bee0d8899e6ee15973f1cff94d47ef8e8cc94d","position":"1788621619517852746-9ea4c2c1-8dd2-4415-8112-6e4c29672829"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"fd990a59b47abe5a52bcb92e9ec2b51e36f735736d5a8f4b7545ddd7e5e8d1c3","event_uuid":"dee3d1a6-70aa-497a-b2da-b9aa4e290e2c","position":{"commit_sha":"a69c904081f4dc6071dd32ca44713d5ab8680c17","position":"1788621733776021286-dee3d1a6-70aa-497a-b2da-b9aa4e290e2c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## RCA evidence for this ticket's acceptance criteria (from incident `bafc-2f85-836f-4bdd` / `decrepit-blowy-javalina`)\n\nTwo answers were requested. The second one **invalidates this ticket's replay criterion as written** — please correct it before anyone implements.\n\n### 1. Observed duplicate count and rate\n\nMeasured over the whole rebar store (5,329 non-archived tickets) and the live binding store (`.bridge_state/bindings.json` @ `origin/tickets`, 5,333 entries):\n\n- **89 normalized titles** have more than one ticket.\n- **425 excess tickets** (total copies minus one per title).\n- **425 of 425 are bound to Jira**, each to a distinct key — Jira range **REB-665..REB-4415**.\n- **389 of the 425** have rebar status != closed, i.e. they are the open Jira duplicates the operator sees.\n- Worst offenders: 12x `a2-1: move last_get_pass rotation bookkeeping...`, 9x each for seven `comment triage: <area>` titles, 8x several `size relief: ...` titles.\n\n**Rate, for threshold-setting:**\n\n| window | excess duplicate tickets created |\n|---|---|\n| 2026-08-31 (whole day) | 233 |\n| 2026-09-01 (whole day) | 172 |\n| peak hour 08-31 23:00Z | 88 |\n| 08-31 06:00Z .. 09-01 04:00Z (the burst) | 345 |\n| typical baseline (Jul-Aug, per day) | 0-2 |\n\nA threshold of **>10 same-normalized-title excess creations per rolling hour** separates the burst (88/hr at peak, 6 consecutive hours above 20) from baseline (0-2/day) with ~an order of magnitude of headroom.\n\n### 2. The duplicate signature — normalized title, as assumed. BUT the replay window is wrong.\n\n**Signature: confirmed normalized title.** All 425 were found by exactly `re.sub(r'\\s+',' ',title.strip().lower())` collision. `create_ticket`'s existing `duplicate_warning` (`_lib_writes.py:182`) uses the same signature and would have fired on every one. No rewrite of the criteria is needed on this axis.\n\nExplicitly ruled out, so nobody has to re-derive it:\n- **Zero** Jira keys are bound to more than one local ticket (5,333 bindings, 5,333 distinct keys). There is no \"one rebar ticket, two Jira issues\" duplicate class.\n- The binding store grew monotonically through the whole incident and never lost an entry, so there is no binding-field-only duplicate class either.\n\n**The replay criterion must change.** The ticket asks the detector to fire against store history for **2026-09-05 05:27-09:26 UTC** (the five long bridge passes). **Zero duplicate-title tickets were created in that window** — or anywhere in the 09-04/09-05 incident at all. A detector replayed there fires zero times and looks broken.\n\nThe correct replay window is **2026-08-31 06:00Z .. 2026-09-01 04:00Z**, where 345 excess creations occurred. Suggested criterion: replayed over that window the detector fires, and replayed over 2026-08-20..08-25 (baseline) it does not.\n\n### 3. A second detector is needed — title collision would NOT have caught this incident\n\nThe 09-04/05 event that produced hundreds of new open Jira issues was **~1,700 tickets with distinct titles** (`Condense comments in <path>`, one per repo file), created 2026-09-04 19:00-01:00Z. Every title is unique, so `duplicate_warning` is silent by construction and correctly so.\n\nThe signal that would have caught it is **creation volume**, not collision:\n\n- rebar side: local CREATE events/hour went 4-9 (steady) -> 62 -> 184 -> **968** -> 318.\n- bridge side: `RECON: outbound_differ create=` went 0-4 (steady) -> 138 -> 520 -> **1180**.\n\nBoth are rebar-side signals — neither needs a Jira query, so neither inherits the ACLI 1,200 ceiling. The `create=` counter in particular is already printed every pass and already thrown away, exactly like `duplicate_warning`.\n\nRecommend this ticket cover **two** detectors, or split the volume one out:\n- **A. Collision detector** — aggregate `duplicate_warning`; threshold >10/rolling hour; replay 08-31 06:00Z..09-01 04:00Z.\n- **B. Volume detector** — alarm on local CREATE events/hour and on per-pass `outbound_differ create=`; threshold ~10x trailing-7-day median; replay 09-04 19:00Z..09-05 02:00Z.\n\nDetector A alone would have missed this incident entirely. That is the \"quietly makes the whole alarm useless\" outcome the ticket was worried about, and it is real — just on the volume axis rather than the signature axis.","timestamp":1788621530184462718}],"created_at":1788621079663951045,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9ea4c2c1-8dd2-4415-8112-6e4c29672829","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"bafc-2f85-836f-4bdd"}],"description":"## The gap\n\nrebar ALREADY detects duplicate creation. `create_ticket` returns a `duplicate_warning` when another\nticket with the same normalized title was created inside a recency window\n(`src/rebar/_lib_writes.py:182`, surfaced through `types.py:264` and `_mcp_writes.py:182`).\n\nBut it is **advisory and per-call**. `_warn_advisory` hands the string back to the caller and that is\nthe end of it. Nothing counts these, publishes a metric, or alarms. So a writer creating hundreds of\nduplicates emits hundreds of individual advisories that no human reads.\n\n## TWO detectors are required, not one — corrected by the RCA\n\nThe 2026-09-05 RCA (`bafc-2f85-836f-4bdd`) established that a title-collision detector **would not\nhave caught the incident that prompted this ticket**. Both signals are needed:\n\n**(a) Duplicate titles.** Confirmed as the right predicate for the duplicate population: all 425\nexcess tickets are found by exactly the normalized-title rule `duplicate_warning` already uses, and\nthat warning would have fired on every one.\n\n**(b) Creation VOLUME.** The ~1,700-ticket surge that drove the Jira flood had **distinct titles**\n(`Condense comments in <path>`, one per repo file), so (a) is blind to it. The signal that would have\ncaught it is rate: local CREATE events/hour went 4-9 -> 62 -> 184 -> **968** -> 318. The per-pass\n`create=` counter in the reconciler's `outbound_differ` is likewise already computed and already\nthrown away (baseline 0-4, surge peak 1180).\n\nBoth are rebar-side, so neither inherits the ACLI 1,200-issue ceiling.\n\n## Why detect in rebar rather than Jira\n\nA Jira-side detector is bounded by the ACLI per-query ceiling — the constraint whose workaround was\ninitially suspected of causing this incident. A detector that can be blinded by the class of defect it\nwatches for is not a detector. rebar's store has no such limit.\n\n## The detector must be independent of the bridge\n\nDo NOT emit these metrics from the reconciler. A malfunctioning bridge must not be responsible for\nreporting its own malfunction — a dead-man inversion this repo has already paid for\n(`herbal-garish-monkey`, `illbred-sour-alpaca`). The bridge runs in GitHub Actions\n(`.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`), so a host-side observer reading the store is independent\nby construction.\n\n## Do not repeat this month's alarm defects\n\n- `undefiled-revivable-gemsbok` — `pct_of_cap` clamps at 100, so cap metrics cannot report the breach\n  they exist to detect. Do not clamp a count or a rate.\n- `illbred-sour-alpaca` — `datapoints_to_alarm = 2` of `evaluation_periods = 3` with\n  `treat_missing_data = \"breaching\"` against a drifting publisher produces alarms that fire on healthy\n  operation and, when the publisher is slow, can never clear. Choose the missing-data policy and M-of-N\n  against THIS metric's measured cadence and justify it.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A duplicate-title metric counts same-normalized-title creations over a window, derived from the\n      SAME rule `duplicate_warning` uses — reuse it, do not invent a second definition that can\n      disagree.\n- [ ] A creation-VOLUME metric counts ticket CREATE events per hour, independent of title. Without\n      this the alarm misses the incident that prompted it.\n- [ ] Both are published by an observer that does NOT depend on the bridge running, demonstrated with\n      reconciliation stopped.\n- [ ] Alarms fire on rates consistent with mass creation, not ordinary operation. Justify against the\n      RCA's real numbers: duplicates baseline 0-2/day against an 88/hr burst, so **>10 per rolling\n      hour** separates them; creation volume baseline 4-9/hr against a 968/hr peak.\n- [ ] `treat_missing_data`, `evaluation_periods` and `datapoints_to_alarm` chosen against measured\n      cadence, with reasoning recorded, and an explicit statement of why the combination cannot\n      reproduce `illbred-sour-alpaca`'s false-page or unclearable-alarm behaviour.\n- [ ] No clamping anywhere in either metric path.\n- [ ] Defect-seeded: synthesise a burst in a test store, confirm each metric rises and its alarm\n      condition is met; remove it and confirm it clears.\n- [ ] Replay proof against the CORRECT window: **2026-08-31 06:00Z - 2026-09-01 04:00Z** (345 excess\n      duplicate tickets; 233 on 08-31, 172 on 09-01) for the duplicate detector, and the\n      **2026-09-04 21:25Z onward** surge for the volume detector. If either would not have fired, the\n      threshold or the signal is wrong — say so rather than adjusting the criterion.\n- [ ] Portability: local store read plus host metric publish; no dependence on any single CI provider.\n\n## Testing\n\n1. RED first: with the detectors absent, show both windows produce no signal.\n2. Unit: the normalized-title rule matches `duplicate_warning`'s, proven by driving both on the same\n   inputs rather than by reading the code.\n3. Replay both historical windows above.\n4. Mutation: break each aggregation independently and confirm a test turns RED for each.\n\n## Provenance\n\nRequested by the operator during the 2026-09-05 incident: \"even with limited Jira query size, we\nshould be able to detect the creation of multiple duplicates in rebar and alarm on the situation.\"\n\n**Correction history:** filed with a single title-based detector and a replay window of 09-05\n05:27-09:26. The RCA established that **zero** duplicates were created in that window and that the\nsurge tickets had distinct titles, so the original spec would have built a detector that missed the\nincident. Both the window and the second detector are corrections from `bafc-2f85-836f-4bdd`.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","bafc-2f85-836f-4bdd"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"dbe7-d957-e5da-49dd","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Duplicate ticket creation is detectable in rebar but nothing aggregates or alarms on it, so a reconciler creating hundreds of duplicates is silent","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["09520870-72ee-431a-bb6d-4439fa31c68f","d9e61719-91f9-4f23-99d4-a4a16ed250bf","9ea4c2c1-8dd2-4415-8112-6e4c29672829","dee3d1a6-70aa-497a-b2da-b9aa4e290e2c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788623684674749001,"uuid":"9b9f1132-35fe-4839-abc2-a1b66295efa7"}